<http://data.silknow.org/object/75b70b97-e749-3898-a4b9-e27b04297873>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk satin. There are two loom widths and a decorative border around the fabric. The design of the central field consists of baskets of flowers with ferns, a group of three putti holding a bird on a piece of string, a bunch of flowers supported by griffins, a pair of crossed arrows tied with ribbon, and two putti emptying pitchers. There are garlands of flowers and cornucopias scattered in the field. In the borders, a group of putti with birds alternates with a bunch of flowers supported by griffins. The design is mainly carried out in soft shades of green, brown, pink and white. The silk is a tissue with a green satin ground, and the pattern is bound in 3/1 twill by a proportion of the threads of the ground warp. There is one white pattern weft. All the other wefts are brocaded."@en , "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk satin, possibly designed by Philippe de Lasalle, France, ca. 1790"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/ab3b5ae0-5644-33f7-8df4-163a10d5183f> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/064eea11-ae07-3642-ba83-68349b1058a4> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/0baa00d2-ff88-3142-8d33-0c50cbe8c49c> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/00753c88-69c1-30ea-a532-32eebdabb119> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk satin, possibly designed by Philippe de Lasalle, France, ca. 1790"@en , "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk satin. There are two loom widths and a decorative border around the fabric. The design of the central field consists of baskets of flowers with ferns, a group of three putti holding a bird on a piece of string, a bunch of flowers supported by griffins, a pair of crossed arrows tied with ribbon, and two putti emptying pitchers. There are garlands of flowers and cornucopias scattered in the field. In the borders, a group of putti with birds alternates with a bunch of flowers supported by griffins. The design is mainly carried out in soft shades of green, brown, pink and white. The silk is a tissue with a green satin ground, and the pattern is bound in 3/1 twill by a proportion of the threads of the ground warp. There is one white pattern weft. All the other wefts are brocaded."@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/75b70b97-e749-3898-a4b9-e27b04297873/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/75b70b97-e749-3898-a4b9-e27b04297873/dimension/4> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/75b70b97-e749-3898-a4b9-e27b04297873/dimension/5> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/75b70b97-e749-3898-a4b9-e27b04297873/dimension/1> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/75b70b97-e749-3898-a4b9-e27b04297873/dimension/3> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.357-1960" ;
